{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And now let it be seen, etc.</b> The reason Joseph made himself an adviser to the king, when the king had asked of him nothing but the interpretation of the dream, is that he wished to give him the reason that HaShem had shown him what He was about to do — for it was in order that he should appoint officers, etc. Further, since they had shown him in the dream that the lean cows swallowed the fat cows, this would indicate that two years of famine would be sustained from two years of plenty. Therefore he said, <b>let Pharaoh look, etc.</b>:" "<b>A man discerning and wise.</b> Discerning — to know the manner of grain storehouses, so that they not rot; this requires discernment. And his saying <b>and wise</b> — one who knows the totality of sciences, to know the science of measurement and engineering and arithmetic. And he placed ״discerning״ first, for it is the more indispensable factor for ensuring that the grain lasts."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:37.356322727Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}